{"timeLimit":2400,"questions":[{"question":"\\(2.75 + .003 - .158\\)","options":["\\(4.36\\)","\\(2.911\\)","\\(2.844\\)","\\(2.938\\)","\\(2.595\\)"],"correctIndex":4,"answer":null,"explanation":["\\(2.750 + 0.003 = 2.753\\); \\(2.753 - 0.158 = 2.595\\)."],"hint":"Line up the decimal points.","image":null,"topic":"Decimals","type":"objective","section":null},{"question":"Which of the following about the values of the digit 8 in \\(1809\\) and \\(687\\) is false?","options":["The place value of the digit 8 in 687 is hundreds","Their place values are not the same","The difference in their values is 720","Their sum is 880","None of the above"],"correctIndex":0,"answer":null,"explanation":["In \\(1809\\) the 8 is worth \\(800\\); in \\(687\\) it is worth \\(80\\) (tens).","So 'the place value of 8 in 687 is hundreds' is false. (The others are true: \\(800 - 80 = 720\\), \\(800 + 80 = 880\\).)"],"hint":"Find what the 8 is worth in each number.","image":null,"topic":"Place Value","type":"objective","section":null},{"question":"What fraction of a week is \\(4\\) days?","options":["\\(\\frac{1}{2}\\)","\\(\\frac{1}{4}\\)","\\(\\frac{4}{7}\\)","\\(\\frac{3}{5}\\)","\\(\\frac{3}{4}\\)"],"correctIndex":2,"answer":null,"explanation":["\\(4\\) days out of \\(7\\) is \\(\\frac{4}{7}\\) of a week."],"hint":"A week has 7 days. (The paper prints 'What fraction of 4 days is a week?'.)","image":null,"topic":"Fractions","type":"objective","section":null},{"question":"The HCF of \\(18\\) and \\(12\\) is","options":["\\(2\\)","\\(7\\)","\\(56\\)","\\(22\\)","\\(6\\)"],"correctIndex":4,"answer":null,"explanation":["\\(6\\) divides \\(18\\) and \\(12\\), and nothing larger does."],"hint":"The largest number that divides both.","image":null,"topic":"HCF and LCM","type":"objective","section":null},{"question":"Express \\(25\\) kobo as a percentage of \\(5\\) naira.","options":["\\(25\\%\\)","\\(2.5\\%\\)","\\(10\\%\\)","\\(5\\%\\)","\\(125\\%\\)"],"correctIndex":3,"answer":null,"explanation":["\\(\\frac{25}{500} \\times 100 = 5\\%\\)."],"hint":"5 naira is 500 kobo.","image":null,"topic":"Percentages","type":"objective","section":null},{"question":"\\(2\\text{ km } 70\\text{ m} \\times d = 1\\text{ km } 35\\text{ m}\\). What is \\(d\\)?","options":["\\(2\\)","\\(\\frac{1}{2}\\)","\\(1\\)","\\(70\\)","\\(35\\)"],"correctIndex":1,"answer":null,"explanation":["\\(2070 \\times d = 1035\\), so \\(d = \\frac{1}{2}\\)."],"hint":"Change both to metres.","image":null,"topic":"Measurement","type":"objective","section":null},{"question":"What is the sum of the squares of \\(4\\), \\(9\\) and \\(11\\)?","options":["\\(250\\)","\\(210\\)","\\(218\\)","\\(26\\)","\\(140\\)"],"correctIndex":2,"answer":null,"explanation":["\\(16 + 81 + 121 = 218\\)."],"hint":"Square each, then add.","image":null,"topic":"Squares","type":"objective","section":null},{"question":"Express in figures: twelve millions, eighteen thousands and four.","options":["\\(120\\,180\\,014\\)","\\(12\\,018\\,004\\)","\\(12\\,001\\,814\\)","\\(12\\,180\\,140\\)","\\(12\\,18\\,014\\)"],"correctIndex":1,"answer":null,"explanation":["\\(12\\,000\\,000 + 18\\,000 + 4 = 12\\,018\\,004\\)."],"hint":"12 000 000 + 18 000 + 4.","image":null,"topic":"Place Value","type":"objective","section":null},{"question":"Find the area of a circle whose diameter is \\(28\\text{ cm}\\). Take \\(\\pi\\) as \\(\\frac{22}{7}\\).","options":["\\(616\\text{ cm}^{2}\\)","\\(154\\text{ cm}^{2}\\)","\\(120\\text{ cm}^{2}\\)","\\(134\\text{ cm}^{2}\\)","\\(134\\text{ cm}^{2}\\)"],"correctIndex":0,"answer":null,"explanation":["\\(r = 14\\): area \\(= \\frac{22}{7} \\times 14 \\times 14 = 616\\text{ cm}^{2}\\)."],"hint":"The radius is half the diameter.","image":null,"topic":"Circles","type":"objective","section":null},{"question":"Simplify \\(17 - 20 \\div 5 + 27\\).","options":["\\(13\\)","\\(6\\)","\\(14\\)","\\(40\\)","\\(30\\)"],"correctIndex":3,"answer":null,"explanation":["\\(20 \\div 5 = 4\\); \\(17 - 4 + 27 = 40\\)."],"hint":"Divide first.","image":null,"topic":"Order of Operations","type":"objective","section":null},{"question":"Find the value of \\(3\\tfrac{1}{3}\\%\\) of \\(\\$1200\\).","options":["\\(660\\)","\\(800\\)","\\(40\\)","\\(132\\)","\\(144\\)"],"correctIndex":2,"answer":null,"explanation":["\\(3\\tfrac{1}{3}\\% = \\frac{1}{30}\\); \\(\\frac{1}{30} \\times 1200 = 40\\)."],"hint":"3⅓% is one thirtieth.","image":null,"topic":"Percentages","type":"objective","section":null},{"question":"What is the LCM of \\(12\\), \\(16\\) and \\(18\\)?","options":["\\(4\\)","\\(24\\)","\\(360\\)","\\(120\\)","\\(144\\)"],"correctIndex":4,"answer":null,"explanation":["\\(12 = 2^{2} \\times 3\\), \\(16 = 2^{4}\\), \\(18 = 2 \\times 3^{2}\\).","LCM \\(= 2^{4} \\times 3^{2} = 144\\)."],"hint":"Highest power of each prime.","image":null,"topic":"HCF and LCM","type":"objective","section":null},{"question":"Write \\(14008\\) in words.","options":["Fourteen and eight","Fourteen thousand eight hundred","Fourteen thousand and eight","Fourteen hundred and eight","One thousand, four hundred and eight"],"correctIndex":2,"answer":null,"explanation":["\\(14\\,008\\) = fourteen thousand and eight."],"hint":"14 thousand and 8.","image":null,"topic":"Place Value","type":"objective","section":null},{"question":"Express \\(₦25\\) as a percentage of \\(₦500\\).","options":["\\(50\\%\\)","\\(40\\%\\)","\\(25\\%\\)","\\(15\\%\\)","\\(5\\%\\)"],"correctIndex":4,"answer":null,"explanation":["\\(\\frac{25}{500} \\times 100 = 5\\%\\)."],"hint":"Divide and multiply by 100.","image":null,"topic":"Percentages","type":"objective","section":null},{"question":"A polygon with \\(12\\) sides is known as","options":["Dodecagon","Undecagon","Decagon","Quadrilateral","Tridecagon"],"correctIndex":0,"answer":null,"explanation":["A 12-sided polygon is a dodecagon."],"hint":"'Dodeca' means twelve.","image":null,"topic":"Polygons","type":"objective","section":null},{"question":"Find the simple interest on \\(₦6400\\) at \\(15\\%\\) for \\(2\\) years.","options":["\\(₦1440\\)","\\(₦1920\\)","\\(₦1200\\)","\\(₦1080\\)","\\(₦600\\)"],"correctIndex":1,"answer":null,"explanation":["\\(\\frac{6400 \\times 15 \\times 2}{100} = ₦1920\\)."],"hint":"I = PRT ÷ 100.","image":null,"topic":"Simple Interest","type":"objective","section":null},{"question":"If \\(a^{2} + b^{2} = c^{2}\\), find \\(a\\) if \\(b = 12\\) and \\(c = 15\\).","options":["\\(3\\)","\\(6\\)","\\(7\\)","\\(9\\)","\\(11\\)"],"correctIndex":3,"answer":null,"explanation":["\\(a^{2} = 225 - 144 = 81\\), so \\(a = 9\\)."],"hint":"a² = c² − b².","image":null,"topic":"Pythagoras","type":"objective","section":null},{"question":"Simplify \\(9\\tfrac{5}{8} \\div 2\\tfrac{3}{4}\\).","options":["\\(3\\tfrac{1}{2}\\)","\\(7\\tfrac{1}{2}\\)","\\(8\\tfrac{1}{3}\\)","\\(9\\tfrac{1}{5}\\)","\\(10\\tfrac{2}{3}\\)"],"correctIndex":0,"answer":null,"explanation":["\\(\\frac{77}{8} \\div \\frac{11}{4} = \\frac{77}{8} \\times \\frac{4}{11} = \\frac{7}{2} = 3\\tfrac{1}{2}\\)."],"hint":"Change to improper fractions, then multiply by the reciprocal.","image":null,"topic":"Fractions","type":"objective","section":null},{"question":"What is the cost of \\(60\\) oranges if \\(4\\) cost \\(₦20\\)?","options":["\\(₦480.00\\)","\\(₦400.00\\)","\\(₦300.00\\)","\\(₦150.00\\)","\\(₦48.00\\)"],"correctIndex":2,"answer":null,"explanation":["One orange costs \\(₦5\\); \\(60 \\times 5 = ₦300\\)."],"hint":"Find the cost of one orange first.","image":null,"topic":"Proportion","type":"objective","section":null},{"question":"A regular rectangular pattern on a wall was created with \\(2\\) kinds of tiles: grey and striped. Some tiles have fallen off the wall (see the picture). How many grey tiles have fallen off?","options":["\\(9\\)","\\(8\\)","\\(7\\)","\\(6\\)","\\(5\\)"],"correctIndex":1,"answer":null,"explanation":["The wall is \\(8\\) tiles wide and \\(5\\) high, grey and striped alternating.","The gap covers \\(4\\) tiles in the second row and \\(6\\) in each of the third and fourth rows.","By the alternating pattern, \\(2 + 3 + 3 = 8\\) of those spaces held grey tiles."],"hint":"The tiles alternate grey and striped like a chessboard: work out which colour belongs in each empty space.","image":"/exam-archive/competitions/scholastic/upper-primary/5th-edition/first-Round/q20.svg","topic":"Patterns","type":"objective","section":null},{"question":"Add three, six and nine.","options":["Sixteen","Seventeen","Eighteen","Twelve","Eighteen"],"correctIndex":2,"answer":null,"explanation":["\\(3 + 6 + 9 = 18\\), eighteen."],"hint":"Add the numbers one at a time.","image":null,"topic":"Basic Arithmetic","type":"objective","section":null},{"question":"The letters in the word MATHEMATICIAN were put in a box. What is the chance of getting letter M?","options":["3 out of 9","3 out of 10","3 out of 13","1 out of 13","2 out of 13"],"correctIndex":4,"answer":null,"explanation":["MATHEMATICIAN has \\(13\\) letters, \\(2\\) of them M.","The chance is \\(2\\) out of \\(13\\)."],"hint":"Count all the letters, then count the M's.","image":null,"topic":"Probability","type":"objective","section":null},{"question":"Taiwo, Kehinde and Idowu are to share \\(\\$600\\) in the ratio \\(3:2:1\\) respectively. What is Kehinde's share?","options":["\\(\\$600\\)","\\(\\$800\\)","\\(\\$100\\)","\\(\\$300\\)","\\(\\$200\\)"],"correctIndex":4,"answer":null,"explanation":["Kehinde gets \\(\\frac{2}{6}\\) of \\(\\$600 = \\$200\\)."],"hint":"There are 6 parts in all.","image":null,"topic":"Ratio","type":"objective","section":null},{"question":"Express \\(40100\\) in standard form.","options":["\\(4.01 \\times 10^{2}\\)","\\(4.01 \\times 10^{-2}\\)","\\(4.01 \\times 10^{4}\\)","\\(4.01 \\times 10^{-4}\\)","\\(4.01 \\times 10^{5}\\)"],"correctIndex":2,"answer":null,"explanation":["\\(40100 = 4.01 \\times 10\\,000 = 4.01 \\times 10^{4}\\)."],"hint":"Move the point until one digit is in front.","image":null,"topic":"Standard Form","type":"objective","section":null},{"question":"Express \\(88\\) as a product of its prime factors in index form.","options":["\\(2^{2} \\times 3 \\times 11\\)","\\(2 \\times 3 \\times 11\\)","\\(2^{3} \\times 11\\)","\\(2^{3} \\times 3 \\times 5 \\times 7\\)","\\(3^{3} \\times 11\\)"],"correctIndex":2,"answer":null,"explanation":["\\(88 = 2 \\times 2 \\times 2 \\times 11 = 2^{3} \\times 11\\)."],"hint":"Keep halving.","image":null,"topic":"Prime Factors","type":"objective","section":null},{"question":"If \\(12\\) men can dig a garden in \\(5\\) days, how many men would be needed to dig it in \\(15\\) days?","options":["\\(6\\)","\\(8\\)","\\(10\\)","\\(12\\)","\\(4\\)"],"correctIndex":4,"answer":null,"explanation":["Work \\(= 12 \\times 5 = 60\\) man-days; in \\(15\\) days it needs \\(4\\) men."],"hint":"More days means fewer men.","image":null,"topic":"Variation","type":"objective","section":null},{"question":"DCCIV represents what number?","options":["\\(704\\)","\\(524\\)","\\(526\\)","\\(606\\)","\\(614\\)"],"correctIndex":0,"answer":null,"explanation":["\\(500 + 100 + 100 + 4 = 704\\)."],"hint":"D = 500, C = 100, IV = 4.","image":null,"topic":"Roman Numerals","type":"objective","section":null},{"question":"What is the minor angle between the hour and minute hand of a clock when it is 10:00?","options":["\\(15^{\\circ}\\)","\\(60^{\\circ}\\)","\\(120^{\\circ}\\)","\\(100^{\\circ}\\)","\\(90^{\\circ}\\)"],"correctIndex":1,"answer":null,"explanation":["At 10:00 the hands are \\(2\\) hour marks apart: \\(2 \\times 30^{\\circ} = 60^{\\circ}\\)."],"hint":"Each hour mark is 30° apart.","image":null,"topic":"Clock Angles","type":"objective","section":null},{"question":"How many VERTICES does a cube have?","options":["\\(4\\)","\\(6\\)","\\(8\\)","\\(2\\)","\\(1\\)"],"correctIndex":2,"answer":null,"explanation":["A cube has \\(8\\) vertices (corners)."],"hint":"Count the corners.","image":null,"topic":"Solids","type":"objective","section":null},{"question":"Divide \\(0.876\\) by \\(7.3\\).","options":["\\(0.4\\)","\\(0.12\\)","\\(0.054\\)","\\(0.14\\)","\\(5.4\\)"],"correctIndex":1,"answer":null,"explanation":["\\(8.76 \\div 73 = 0.12\\)."],"hint":"Multiply both by 10 first.","image":null,"topic":"Decimals","type":"objective","section":null},{"question":"A triangle in which three sides are equal is called ____ triangle.","options":[],"correctIndex":null,"answer":"an equilateral triangle","explanation":["A triangle with all three sides equal is an equilateral triangle."],"hint":"","image":null,"topic":"Triangles","type":"subjective","section":null},{"question":"The perimeter of a rectangle is \\(100\\text{ cm}\\) and its breadth is \\(14\\text{ cm}\\). Find the length.","options":[],"correctIndex":null,"answer":"\\(36\\text{ cm}\\)","explanation":["\\(2(l + 14) = 100\\), so \\(l + 14 = 50\\) and \\(l = 36\\text{ cm}\\)."],"hint":"","image":null,"topic":"Mensuration","type":"subjective","section":null},{"question":"A man walks at \\(8\\text{ km/h}\\). How far does he walk between 9:30 am and 12 noon?","options":[],"correctIndex":null,"answer":"\\(20\\text{ km}\\)","explanation":["9:30 am to 12 noon is \\(2\\tfrac{1}{2}\\) hours; \\(8 \\times 2.5 = 20\\text{ km}\\)."],"hint":"","image":null,"topic":"Speed, Distance and Time","type":"subjective","section":null},{"question":"Observe the pie chart given below. The central angle for sector B is?","options":[],"correctIndex":null,"answer":"\\(144^{\\circ}\\)","explanation":["Sector B is \\(40\\%\\) of the chart.","\\(40\\%\\) of \\(360^{\\circ} = 144^{\\circ}\\)."],"hint":"","image":"/exam-archive/competitions/scholastic/upper-primary/5th-edition/first-Round/q34.svg","topic":"Statistics","type":"subjective","section":null},{"question":"Michael chose some positive number, multiplied it by itself, added \\(1\\), multiplied the result by \\(10\\), added \\(3\\), and multiplied the result by \\(4\\). His final answer was \\(2012\\). What number did Michael choose?","options":[],"correctIndex":null,"answer":"\\(7\\)","explanation":["Work backwards: \\(2012 \\div 4 = 503\\); \\(503 - 3 = 500\\); \\(500 \\div 10 = 50\\); \\(50 - 1 = 49\\).","\\(49 = 7 \\times 7\\), so he chose \\(7\\)."],"hint":"","image":null,"topic":"Number Puzzles","type":"subjective","section":null},{"question":"The base of a triangle is twice the height of the triangle. If the area is \\(16\\) square inches, what is the height?","options":[],"correctIndex":null,"answer":"\\(4\\) inches","explanation":["Area \\(= \\frac{1}{2} \\times 2h \\times h = h^{2} = 16\\).","\\(h = 4\\) inches."],"hint":"","image":null,"topic":"Mensuration","type":"subjective","section":null},{"question":"George left home at 7:30 a.m. for school. School begins at 8:15 a.m. George was \\(10\\) minutes late. How long did George take to get to school?","options":[],"correctIndex":null,"answer":"\\(55\\) minutes","explanation":["He arrived at 8:25 a.m.","7:30 to 8:25 is \\(55\\) minutes."],"hint":"","image":null,"topic":"Time","type":"subjective","section":null},{"question":"Line segments PQ and RS intersect at T, as shown. If TS = TQ and \\(\\angle PTR = 88^{\\circ}\\), the value of \\(x\\) is?","options":[],"correctIndex":null,"answer":"\\(46^{\\circ}\\)","explanation":["\\(\\angle STQ = \\angle PTR = 88^{\\circ}\\) (vertically opposite).","TS = TQ, so the angles at S and Q are equal: \\(x = \\frac{180 - 88}{2} = 46^{\\circ}\\)."],"hint":"","image":"/exam-archive/competitions/scholastic/upper-primary/5th-edition/first-Round/q38.svg","topic":"Angles","type":"subjective","section":null},{"question":"Calculate \\(\\frac{1}{2} - \\frac{3}{5} + \\frac{7}{10}\\).","options":[],"correctIndex":null,"answer":"\\(\\frac{3}{5}\\)","explanation":["Over \\(10\\): \\(\\frac{5 - 6 + 7}{10} = \\frac{6}{10} = \\frac{3}{5}\\)."],"hint":"","image":null,"topic":"Fractions","type":"subjective","section":null},{"question":"What is the ratio of \\(1\\) hour to \\(300\\) seconds?","options":[],"correctIndex":null,"answer":"\\(12 : 1\\)","explanation":["\\(1\\) hour \\(= 3600\\) seconds; \\(3600 : 300 = 12 : 1\\)."],"hint":"","image":null,"topic":"Ratio","type":"subjective","section":null}]}